Certificates and a CRL for tests/x509_total_test.b, which decodes them,
verifies them, and then does both again to some thousands of changed
copies.  Made by tests/host/x509_chain/gen.py -f tests/certs/total
(python3 with the cryptography package); kept here because the test
runs where there is no python.  Valid from 2026 to 2049; the test
verifies at a time of its own.  The keys were thrown away: none of
these is a trust anchor anywhere but inside that test.

  root      CA (P-256) with nameConstraints: permitted dNSName and
            directoryName subtrees, excluded iPAddress (v4 and v6),
            dNSName and directoryName subtrees
  inter     CA under root: pathlen 0, critical certificatePolicies with
            a qualifier, policyMappings, policyConstraints,
            inhibitAnyPolicy, authority and subject key identifiers
  leaf      under inter: a subjectAltName with one name of each form
            (dNSName, a wildcard, iPAddress v4 and v6, rfc822Name, URI,
            an otherName, a directoryName), extendedKeyUsage, keyUsage,
            an authorityKeyIdentifier in its long form, a CRL
            distribution point and an extension nobody knows
  crl       root's, two entries with reason codes, cRLNumber
  rsaroot   CA (RSA 2048, sha256WithRSAEncryption); rsaleaf under it
